* {{IPA|en|/ˌeɪ.bi.ˈsi.dɚ.i/|/ˌeɪ.bi.ˈsi.də.ɹi/|a=US}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|abscedary}}, from {{der|en|ML.|abecedārium||alphabet, ABC primer}}, from {{der|en|LL.|abecedārius||of the alphabet}}, formed from the first four letters of the Latin alphabet + {{m|la|-ārius|}}.<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=3}}</ref> {{doublet|en|abecedarium}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|rare}} The [[alphabet]], written out in a teaching book, or carved on a wall; a primer; [[abecedarium]]. {{defdate|from 1350 to 1470}}<ref name=SOED/>
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=07/18/14|author=Caity Weaver|title=My 14-Hour Search for the End of TGI Friday's Endless Appetizers|work=w:Gawker|url=https://www.gawker.com/my-14-hour-search-for-the-end-of-tgi-fridays-endless-ap-1606122925|passage=I finish writing the alphabet on both napkins. There's room for more '''abecedaries''', but {{...}}|accessdate=17 May 2022|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220516004904/https://www.gawker.com/my-14-hour-search-for-the-end-of-tgi-fridays-endless-ap-1606122925|archivedate=16 May 2022}}
# One that teaches or learns the alphabet or the fundamentals of any subject; [[abecedarian]]. {{defdate|from late 16<sup>th</sup> century}}<ref name=SOED/>

